:: Task Mom Test Session 0 [task_scene] {"position":"2025,3925"}
/* Scene of the task "Test Session", stage 0 (sessions 1 to 3). Played every time the task starts while I'm in the meeting room.
   Unlocked by the quest "Can you help me a little more?" (mom_testSessionRequest). Effects are in the task's onComplete.
   Stage 0 sets the rules. On the first night she talked, apologized and fanned herself, and now I start cutting that out:
   a number and nothing else, both hands on the table, and she answers the last question to me instead of to the box.
   The later stages come back to these rules, and by then she keeps them without being told.
   Only the top of her blouse opens, and only after she asks. I never touch her. */
<<silent>>
	<<SetBackground $locations[15].img>>
	<<set _ts0Task to setup.getTaskById("task_mom_test_session")>>
	<<set _ts0First to (_ts0Task.count || 0) === 0>>
	<<set _ts0 to random(0, 2)>>
<</silent>>
<<= either(
"The office empties out the usual way. $ethan.name leaves last, announcing that he's going home to 'touch grass', and $brian.name leaves without announcing anything, which is how he always leaves.",
"$darius.name is the last to go tonight. He stops at the meeting room door, sees the white box and the questionnaire on the table, and says he'd love to see the numbers once there are enough of them. I tell him he will. He won't.",
"It rained all afternoon, and the windows of the meeting room are still beaded with it. Somebody left half a sandwich on the table. I throw it away before $mom.callName gets here, because she'd make a whole thing out of it."
)>>

$mom.callName comes in with the questionnaire already on a clipboard and two pens, like always. <<= either(
"She's brought tea and offers me a sip. I say no. She tells me it's chamomile, as if that's going to change my mind.",
"She's let her hair down since this afternoon, and she keeps tucking the same strand behind her ear while she sits down.",
"She's taken off her heels and carries them in one hand, and once she's sitting she tucks her feet up onto the seat like she's settling in for a movie."
)>>

<<if _ts0First>>
On the first night I let her talk as much as she liked, because I needed her to come back for a second one. She came back. Tonight I pull the clipboard over to my side of the table before she can get comfortable.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I want to change one thing from last time. When I ask you something, just give me the number, okay? No story to go with it." },
{ who: $mom, text: "No story? Sweetie, half of what I say is context." },
{ who: $player, text: "I know, and I like the context, but there's no column for it on the sheet." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Well, there should be. How is anybody supposed to tell one six from another six?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Just the number, $mom.callName. Please." },
{ text: "She has something to say about my tone. I watch her fold it up and put it away for later, the same way she folds the dish towels, corners first." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Fine, a number it is. Yes, sir." },
{ text: "She says it as a joke, with a little salute of the pen. I don't correct her." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<else>>
She remembers the rule. I can tell because she sits down, opens her mouth, and closes it again, and her first sentence of the evening stays somewhere behind her teeth.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: either("Am I allowed to say hello, or is that context?", "I'm not going to talk. Look at me, this is me not talking, and I'm very good at it.", "I practiced in the car, you know. Six. Seven. Eight. See? Not a single word in between.") },
{ who: $player, text: either("Hello is fine. Anything after hello is context.", "Very convincing. Let's see how long it lasts.", "I'll count that as your warm-up.") },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Switch it on">>
The blue light comes on and starts its slow pulse. Under the table, my phone is already on her profile. <<DevicePulse 1>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Calm, one to ten." },
{ who: $mom, text: either("Five.", "Six.", "Seven.") },
{ text: "And then, because she can't help herself:" },
{ who: $mom, text: either("Somebody parked across my spot this morning, and I've been...", "$boss.callName's office put me on hold for twenty minutes, and the music was...", "$sister.callName sent me a picture of a dog, and it had these...") },
{ who: $player, text: "That was a lot more than a number." },
{ who: $mom, text: "The number came first, honey. The rest was free." },
{ text: "I write it down and nudge the slider up. Not far. The point of a test is the difference." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<silently>>
<<DevicePulse "+1">>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "How focused?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "Six. Seven. Six." },
{ text: "The 'sorry' is right there, I can see it coming. She catches it and presses her lips together." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

We get through $darius.name's twelve questions faster than she's used to, because nothing is slowing us down anymore. She still has opinions about the wording of question four. She keeps them to herself and lets me read them off her face instead, which is quicker anyway.

<<linkreplace "Turn it up a notch">>
Around question nine, I give the slider that isn't on $darius.name's sheet a little more than last time. <<DevicePulse "+1">>

It reaches her from the outside in, the way it always does. Her cheeks go first, then her throat. She picks up the clipboard to fan herself with it.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Put the clipboard down, please." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Honey, it's like a greenhouse in here. I'm not fanning myself for fun, you could grow tomatoes on this table." },
{ who: $player, text: "I know it's warm. Put it down anyway, and keep both hands on the table." },
{ text: "She looks at me over the top of the clipboard for a long second. Then she lays it down and puts her hands flat on either side of it, fingers spread, like she's waiting for her nail polish to dry." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Like this? Or is that too much finger?" },
{ who: $player, text: "That's good. Just leave them there." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<if setup.corruptionTotal("mom") gte 30>>
She gets the top button of her blouse open before she remembers where her hands are supposed to be. Her fingers stop on the second one, and she looks across at me the way I used to look at her when I'd reached across the dinner table for the salt.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Go on, that one too." },
{ text: "She undoes the second button. Then the hand goes back to the table, exactly where it was, and smooths the sheet flat, as if that's what it got up to do in the first place." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<else>>
She lasts two more questions.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Can I at least undo a button? Just the top one, honey, I'm melting, and it's only you, you've seen me in my bathrobe with that green mask on my face." },
{ text: "I let her wait. I write something on the sheet that doesn't need writing, and I take my time over it." },
{ who: $player, text: "One button. The top one." },
{ text: "She undoes one, puts her hand back on the table, and says thank you. I don't think she hears herself say it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<</if>>

That leaves the last question, the one in pencil at the bottom of the sheet.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "How attractive do you feel right now?" },
{ who: $mom, text: either("Honey, $darius.name should be ashamed of himself for that one.", "Oh, this one again. Can't we skip this one, just once?", "In this blouse? After the day I've had? Ask me on a Saturday.") },
{ who: $player, text: "That's very nice, but it isn't a number." },
{ text: "She laughs and turns to the box, the way she did on the first night, like it might answer for her." },
{ who: $player, text: "Look at me when you say it, not at the box." },
{ text: "Her eyes come off the blue light and find mine, and it takes her a moment to get them to stay there." },
{ who: $mom, text: either("Seven.", "Seven. Seven and a half?", "Eight. Is that too high? That feels too high, doesn't it?") },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She doesn't watch me write it down tonight. She keeps looking at me, because nobody told her she could stop.

<<linkreplace "Wrap it up">>
I switch off the box and let everything else drift back down under the table. <<DevicePulse "off">> It takes her a minute to come back up. It takes a little longer each time, though I haven't put that on any sheet.

Her hands stay on the table until I tell her she can have her pens back.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: ["Was that better? I only slipped twice, and one of those was a sneeze.", "Same time next week, then? I could bring those lemon bars from the bakery, the ones $sister.callName always steals...", "Is it terrible that I look forward to these? I catch myself checking the clock at my desk around four."][_ts0] },
{ who: $player, text: ["Much better. I didn't count the sneeze.", "Whenever it's in the schedule. I'll let you know.", "It's not terrible. It's actually good for the data."][_ts0] },
{ who: $mom, text: ["Oh, good. I was sure you were going to dock me for question four.", "Of course you'll let me know. I'll bring the lemon bars anyway, they don't count as context.", "Well, then I'll keep doing it. For the data."][_ts0] },
{ who: $player, text: either("And next time, be here at seven, not ten to. I'd like to start on time.", "And next time, come straight from your desk. Don't go home to change first.", "And next time, your phone stays in your bag. I could hear it buzzing the whole time.") },
{ who: $mom, text: "Yes, sir." },
{ text: "She's made that joke before. This time she forgets the salute." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

At the door she does up the button I let her open and smooths down her blouse with both hands. Then she says goodnight to the box. She's started doing that every time.

<<EndTaskScene>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
